I am pretty sure that you need a CD-rom that supports 512 byte blocksize=20
for this to work in your alpha. Most of them only do 2048 bytes and I have=
=20
never had any success with those. The symptoms of not using 512 bytes=20
blocksize have been exactly those you've had. This does not not seem=20
to apply if you have a regular ISO formatted cd.

You should also be able to test the cd's before trying to boot from them.=
=20
With the cdhdtape written to it is possible to mount the cd just like if=20
it was a harddrive (with -ro since it is readonly media) and disklabel=20
should show what slices are on there just like with any regular disk.

Cheers,
Anders

